WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.360
We are in an epidemic of bigorexia
and male body dysmorphia -

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.080
men who look in the mirror and
see either Peperamis or blobs,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.280
rather than the medium-sized body
they’ve probably got.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.440
I’m talking about men descending
into the equivalent of anorexia.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.640
Bigorexia. Neurosis about
the way we look.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.800
Looking in the mirror
and seeing what isn’t you.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.440
Going after an unrealistic goal that
can ultimately damage your health.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.560
On my latest lads’ holiday,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.160
five of my friends
refused to take their T-shirts off

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.880
because they were insecure
about how they looked.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.240
Back in my dad’s day it was like,
man boobs out, bombing the pool.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.800
Steroid usage, massively prevalent.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.920
Just look at the reality TV shows -

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.440
you can’t get that body just
from doing a little bit of cardio.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.080
If you think I’m just being dramatic,

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.520
we live in an era where
male suicide is at its highest.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.560
Male eating disorders are on
the rise. This is a huge thing.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:05.600
Men are looking in the mirror
and their brains are tripping out.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:06.640
The end result,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.320
Cardiff high street is full of people

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.160
that look like they were
made by the X-Men.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.040
These are men injecting themselves.
This is bigorexia in action.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.200
I ask these men,
they say back to me...

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.680
"Women want a big strong bloke
that’ll lift them up.”

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.080
Sometimes they drop into morse code -

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.560
dot, dot, dash, dot, dot,
dash, testosterone,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.080
dot, dot, dash.
Meat, metal, football.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.320
Listen ladies, I don’t presume
to understand what women want.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.160
But mostly, gentlemen,

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.320
the primary characteristic
that a woman is looking for

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.800
is a man that isn’t an arse -

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.160
something that will be made
much, much worse

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.640
if you inject yourself
with steroids. Ironically.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.360
Bigorexia is not new.
It has come in several phases.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.720
It started with Joe Weider
and Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.480
when bodybuilding
exploded years ago.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.920
My dad was heavily involved.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.400
My dad’s neck
was bigger than my thigh.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:00.640
It’s true though.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.560
I’m not suggesting we shouldn’t
eat healthily, be a bit toned,

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.960
do some exercise,
make an effort, gents.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.560
Everyone likes that.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.200
What I’m suggesting is,
in our culture,

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.760
it can be a bit of a turn off
to be a bit too perfect.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.400
I know it goes against everything we
know about Darwinian evolution,

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.720
but British people are not
attracted to perfection.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.320
It made me the opposite
of my old man.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.040
He was 17 stone, shaven-headed,
doorman, metal welder, lifeguard,

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.160
semi-competitive bodybuilding
oiled athlete nut job,

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.480
and he had me for a son -

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.080
a skinny Peperami stick with a
glittery question mark over the top:

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.840
“I quite like theatre, daddy.”

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.480
But I do have a connection to this.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.120
I’ve never used steroids myself.
Really, Poirot?

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.600
But my dad did.
My dad massively used steroids.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.520
He injected it.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.080
He lifted massively heavy weights,

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.920
and it turned his aortic valve, the
one that looks like a Mercedes sign,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.760
into a bicuspid
double triangular flap.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.480
That could happen to you gentlemen.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.040
So instead of three flaps opening

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.240
every time you breathe
in and out, two.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.920
And over the years it sticks,
sticks, sticks, sticks

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.880
and if you make it to 60,
you’ll be lucky.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.360
That’s what happened to my dad.
Heart attack, boom. Gone. Very sad.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:10.800
The only up side?

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.800
I can now do stand-up about
him and pay my mortgage.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.280
Stay healthy, gents.

